# cosm's system files. /update replaces exactly these; everything else is the user's.
# Rules for writing them:
# - Name no product or vendor; describe a tool by what it does ("a mail tool").
#   Exception: adapters for one tool (CLAUDE.md, .claude/, .claudian/).
# - Write "the user" and "the agent", never a name.
# - AGENTS.md loads every session: keep it short.
# - The user's own Obsidian choices are not listed: appearance.json (light/dark), community-plugins.json,
#   Style Settings' data.json (theme flavour). A version that must change one says so in CHANGES.md and asks.
# - A file the user also changes (Claudian's settings, app.json, plugin settings, settings.local.json) is not listed:
#   cosm's own keys in it are in .claude/scripts/settings.json, which /update merges in, key by key.
# - A change to the folder layout gets a step in cosm.sh update_migrate, so earlier vaults update instead of reinstalling.
# source: https://github.com/emnl/cosm
